 RecordIndexNowPing(registryPath indexStamp noOfUrls);ns
⍝ Notes what was last announced to IndexNow; see `PingIndexNow` for the fields.
⍝ `indexStamp` is what the index file's timestamp was when the announcement was prepared, so
⍝ that a package published while it was going out is announced next time rather than missed.
 ns←⎕NS''
 ns.indexStamp←indexStamp
 ns.lastPing←Reg.FormatFloatDate⊃60 ⎕DT⊂⎕TS         ⍝ Same shape as a publishing date, so the two compare
 ns.pinged←noOfUrls
 ((Reg.JSON ns)'UTF-8')⎕NPUT(GetIndexNowFilename registryPath)1
⍝Done
